{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 28, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e2b-it", "content": "The morning sun felt… different. Not just the warmth on his skin, but the way the light refracted through the leaves of the oak tree outside his window – too perfect, too symmetrical. He sat up in bed, a strange awareness blooming in his chest. His bedroom wasn't his bedroom. The furniture was oddly stylized, the colors vibrant and almost aggressively cheerful. A pixelated bird chirped outside, its song a synthesized melody that grated on his nerves. He reached for his phone, expecting the usual news headlines, but the screen displayed a loading icon. Panic tightened his throat. He looked at his hands, flexing his fingers, noticing the subtle, almost unnatural smoothness of the skin. This wasn’t real. It couldn't be.\n\n***\n\nHe stumbled out of bed, the floor feeling strangely springy beneath his feet. The hallway was lined with identical doors, each adorned with a glowing emblem he didn't recognize. A small, robotic drone zipped past, its voice a cheerful, pre-recorded greeting. \"Welcome to Aethelgard, citizen! Please proceed to your designated sector.\" Aethelgard. The name echoed in his mind, a stark confirmation of his horrifying realization. He was inside a video game. He had to figure out how to get out, how to break free from this meticulously crafted, utterly artificial world. The cheerful drone continued its programmed route, oblivious to the desperate, bewildered man it was about to encounter. His life, everything he knew, was now a code, a quest, a level he didn't understand.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "The", "logprob": -0.6412928104400635}, {"token": "▁morning", "logprob": -1.4735186100006104}, {"token": "▁sun", "logprob": -0.0766761526465416}, {"token": "▁felt", "logprob": -0.4915617108345032}, {"token": "…", "logprob": -0.03263773024082184}, {"token": "▁different", "logprob": -2.5884006023406982}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -7.9869905